{"Hello? Is someone there?": [0.0, 2.304], "Oh. Good. Nobody picks up anymore.": [2.704, 2.987], "Then who picked up?": [6.091, 1.259], "Maybe. That’s what everyone says in the fog.": [7.749, 3.285], "Are you alone in the room?": [11.435, 2.261], "No. You’re not.": [14.096, 1.408], "I know. I can see it too.": [15.904, 2.539], "That’s the right answer.": [18.843, 1.664], "Do you want to know where Ruth went?": [20.907, 2.304], "Then listen carefully.": [23.611, 2.133], "You will.": [26.144, 0.929], "Everyone wants to know, in the end.": [27.473, 2.901], "Put out the lantern. Then look at the window. Whatever is written there, type it into the terminal. Will you do that for me?": [30.775, 6.805], "Good. I’ll be listening.": [37.98, 1.984], "You will anyway. Everyone does.": [40.364, 2.56], "Then I’ll wait. I’m good at waiting.": [43.324, 2.688], "Did you type what the window said into the terminal?": [46.412, 3.563], "Then the band would be open. You’re lying to me. That’s alright. Everyone lies at three twelve.": [50.375, 5.611], "Type it. Exactly as it’s written.": [56.385, 2.859], "The terminal remembers, even if you don’t.": [59.644, 3.136], "Is the lantern out?": [63.18, 1.664], "Good. Then you can read the glass.": [65.244, 2.453], "Put it out. The writing only shows in the dark.": [68.097, 3.456], "You’d know. You’d feel the room get colder.": [71.953, 2.901], "Will you type it now, while I wait?": [75.255, 2.709], "I’ll be right here. I’m always right here.": [78.364, 2.987], "Then I’ll call again. And again.": [81.751, 2.688], "Maybe is what Ruth said, too.": [84.839, 2.624], "The band with no name is open. Did you find the numbers yet?": [87.863, 4.181], "Then you know where she is.": [92.444, 2.261], "Short wave. Somebody reads them every night, after four chimes.": [95.105, 4.437], "Listen for four chimes.": [99.943, 2.368], "When you find her, will you tell her I’m still waiting?": [102.711, 3.413], "Thank you. She’ll know my voice.": [106.524, 2.624], "Then I’ll tell her myself. Someday.": [109.548, 3.008], "She used to say maybe, too.": [112.956, 2.56], "Are you afraid of what you’ll hear?": [115.916, 2.539], "Good. That means you’re listening.": [118.855, 2.432], "You should be. A little.": [121.687, 2.112], "Turn the dial slowly.": [124.199, 2.283], "Is the lantern still lit?": [126.881, 2.24], "Put it out. It’s easier to see in the dark.": [129.521, 3.2], "Good. Now look at the window.": [133.121, 2.347], "You don’t know? Look at it.": [135.868, 1.877], "Do you know who lit it first?": [138.145, 2.091], "Then you know he never came back from the rocks.": [140.636, 3.221], "The lighthouse keeper. Nineteen oh four. He went down to answer the knocking.": [144.257, 4.821], "Ask the radio. Station forty nine remembers.": [149.479, 3.755], "If something knocks tonight, will you answer it?": [153.633, 3.221], "Don’t. Please. Not tonight.": [157.255, 2.389], "Good. Keep it that way.": [160.044, 2.176], "Then keep the lantern close.": [162.62, 2.368], "Have you seen them? Down in the street?": [165.388, 2.837], "They’ve seen you too.": [168.625, 1.6], "Look again. Under the streetlight.": [170.625, 2.56], "That means yes.": [173.585, 1.451], "Do you want them to come inside?": [175.436, 2.56], "Don’t say that. Not even as a joke.": [178.396, 2.88], "Then keep the window shut.": [181.676, 2.197], "They heard maybe.": [184.273, 1.472], "Is your window open right now?": [186.145, 2.688], "Close it. Quietly.": [189.233, 2.069], "Good. Check the latch.": [191.703, 1.877], "Go and look. I’ll wait.": [193.98, 1.963], "Do you like the radio?": [196.343, 1.643], "She’ll be glad.": [198.385, 1.195], "She can hear you, you know.": [199.98, 2.24], "Turn it on anyway. She gets lonely.": [202.62, 3.115], "Have you heard station thirteen?": [206.135, 2.731], "That was her song. She played it every night.": [209.265, 3.029], "Turn to thirteen. It’s playing right now. It’s always playing.": [212.695, 4.181], "You’d remember. Everyone remembers that song.": [217.276, 3.307], "Do you know the words?": [220.983, 1.429], "Then sing them. Softly. Someone might hear.": [222.812, 3.285], "No place like home. That’s all you need to know.": [226.497, 3.371], "They’ll come back to you. At three twelve.": [230.268, 2.987], "Are you still there?": [233.655, 1.451], "Stay. Please stay.": [235.505, 1.813], "Then who is breathing?": [237.719, 1.792], "Me too.": [239.911, 0.954], "Do you hear that? In the background?": [241.265, 2.624], "That’s the harbor. The water is very close tonight.": [244.289, 3.563], "Listen harder.": [248.252, 1.365], "It’s the bells. Thirty one of them.": [250.017, 2.752], "Will you call me if you need me?": [253.169, 2.389], "You can’t. The line was cut in nineteen sixty one. I’ll call you.": [255.958, 4.608], "I’ll call you anyway.": [260.966, 1.707], "I’ll be waiting by the phone.": [263.073, 2.389], "Has the terminal told you what it is?": [265.862, 2.944], "Then you know it’s the third. There were others.": [269.206, 2.965], "Ask it. Ask it what it is.": [272.572, 2.624], "It tells everyone, eventually.": [275.596, 2.731], "Do you know about the vault?": [278.726, 1.856], "Then don’t say its name on this line.": [280.982, 2.944], "Good. Some things are better left in the vault.": [284.326, 3.157], "Ask the terminal about Null.": [287.884, 2.667], "Are you a member of the Null Membership Society?": [290.95, 3.52], "Then welcome home.": [294.87, 1.728], "Not yet.": [296.998, 1.054], "The Null Membership Society never says maybe.": [298.453, 3.691], "Ruth is gone. Someone has to stay on the air. Will you stay?": [302.543, 4.096], "Yes. You will.": [307.039, 1.259]}